# The assets directory is the repository root, so this file decides what
# the site publishes. It is an allowlist: everything is left out, then the
# site's own files are let back in. A new page or image at the root is
# public by its extension; a new directory has to be named here. Source,
# tooling, docs and anything untracked in a working copy stay private.
/*
!/*.html
!/*.css
!/*.png
!/*.ico
!/*.svg
!/*.txt
!/*.xml
!/*.webmanifest
!/assets/
!/data/
!/fonts/
!/modules/

# Inside those: the notes for whoever edits them, and macOS's folder files.
README.md
.DS_Store
